## Context

dyne replicates erg's four documentation layers with shared machinery
and per-tool artifacts (0270, implementation scheme). This ticket wires
layers 2-4 around the 0273 binary.

## Scope

- `dyne init`: unpack into `tickets/merges/` -- `AGENTS.md` (embedded asset),
  `.gitattributes` with `merge=union` on `tickets/merges/*.dyne`, a `.dynerc`
  skeleton (`[hooks]`); the init-unpack ASCII guard applies to every
  unpacked asset (0245 precedent)
- `dyne spec` and `dyne integration` served from embedded assets: the
  %dyne 0.1 spec (0272) and the composition-seam guide (hooks, opaque
  `Closes:` refs, the `add -A` staging clause)
- `make docs` gains `dyne --help --all > docs/dyne-manual.md`; the
  manual cannot drift because it is the binary's own help output
- self-coherence guard: CI fails when the deployed `tickets/merges/AGENTS.md`
  drifts from the embedded source, mirroring erg's guard; fold a
  `dyne check tickets/merges/` gate into `make test` (0246 precedent)

## Historical exit criteria

These criteria are candidates only. Before work starts, revise them to match
the decision in 0271; if Dyne is not justified, do not implement them.

- [ ] `dyne init` on a fresh repo yields a working store, offline
- [ ] guards live in `make test`, not only CI

## Design reassessment (2026-11-04)

Git notes are the review-evidence store, as the author confirmed. The earlier
`tickets/reviews/` proposal is superseded. Read `docs/dyne-review-contract.md`
for the current harness evidence and the remaining decision. The scope above
records the original design candidates; it does not authorize implementation.
Ticket 0271 must first establish a concrete unmet need and decide whether a
separate Dyne object is warranted. Subsequent format and implementation work
is conditional on that decision. This ticket remains open.
